---
import { url } from '../../lib/url';

interface Props {
  h1: string;
}

const { h1 } = Astro.props;
---
  <h1>{h1}</h1>

<h2 id="resumen">Summary <i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i> </h2>

<p>
  Website where board games can be posted for sale and purchase. Users can 
  write comments on the products and rate them with stars.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>GitHub repository <i class="fab fa-github"></i>:</strong>
  <a href="https://github.com/Franco2900/Practica-1---Tienda-juegos-de-mesa" target="_blank">Practice 1</a>
</p>

<h2 id="tecnologias">Technologies used <i class="bi bi-laptop"></i> </h2>

<div class="row">

  <div class="col-4">
    Backend:<br>
    NodeJS <i class="fab fa-node-js"></i> with the Express framework
  </div>

  <div class="col-4">
    Database:<br>
    SQL <i class="fas fa-database"></i>
  </div>
  
  <div class="col-4">
    Frontend:<br>
    Bootstrap <i class="fab fa-bootstrap"></i> and EJS
  </div>
  
</div>
<br>

<h2 id="descripcion">Full project description <i class="fas fa-align-left"></i> </h2>

<p>
  Whenever I did practice projects, they were meant to create small pieces of code and understand how
  a concept, a feature or a module works. The big projects I did were always for university and in groups.
  That is why this is my first big project built entirely by me.<br />

  &emsp;&emsp;Store websites are one of the first things people practice, and since I really like
  board games, one day I decided to make a website as if I were a seller of these products.<br />

  &emsp;&emsp;Below is a complete description of all the features available on the website.
  To start, the site is divided into the following sections: Home; 
  Products, which in turn is split into Buy and Sell; Contact, with all the ways to get in touch and a FAQ;
  Log in and Register, to access the account; and finally Profile, where the user can
  change their name, password and profile picture.<br />

  &emsp;&emsp;Unregistered visitors can only see the Buy section to browse the available products,
  but they can't interact until they log in. Registered users with the regular user role can
  buy products, give them a rating of up to 5 stars (the system automatically updates each
  product's overall rating every time a user rates it), buy one or several products at a
  time, leave comments and reply to other users' comments. Admins have the same
  features as a regular user, plus the ability to publish new items for sale.
</p>


