<h2 id="aprendizaje">What I learned <i class="fas fa-graduation-cap"></i> </h2>
<p>
  • Routing — Process of defining the routes of a web application, indicating which content or action runs based on the requested URL. <br />
  • GET and POST methods — Ways to send data between client and server: GET to retrieve information and POST to send or modify data. <br />
  • EJS — Template engine that lets you embed JavaScript in HTML to generate dynamic pages. <br />
  • Middleware — Intermediate functions that process requests before they reach the controller, useful for validation, authentication or error handling. <br />
  • Connecting to and working with a database — Integration of the application with data storage systems (such as SQL or NoSQL) to save, query and update information. <br />
  • User session management — Mechanism to keep a user's information while they browse the application, such as their login state or preferences. <br />
</p>